    "body": "Relay BB run pushed an update.\n\nPull request: #333\n\nTokens: 0 · Cost: $0.0000\n\nPushed branch `bb/relay-127-mcp-integration-06-07-manage-project-m-thr_dggg25qrdi` to origin.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplements issue #127: management of project-level MCP tool grants (the \"Tools block\").\n\n- **Backend** (`@semprec/data`): `mcpAgentPageGrants.ts` adds the read model (`listMcpToolGrantsForProject`, joining registrations with server identity and this project's grant, default unchecked) and write wrappers (`setProjectMcpGrantForAgentPage`, `reclassifyMcpTool`). These wrappers live inside the package so the admin-only mutations in `mcpGrantsAdminStore.ts` stay unreachable from `agent-runtime`'s public import surface — an existing security boundary in this codebase.\n- **HTTP API** (`semprec-api`): `mcpAgentPageHandler.ts`, bearer-token authenticated, exposing GET/PATCH for project grants and PATCH for tool reclassification, routed alongside the existing AI-usage handler.\n- **Frontend**: `mcpAgentPageOperations.ts` (zod-validated client) and `ToolsBlock.tsx`, a self-contained component grouping tools by server with a checkbox bound to the project's grant, plus risk-class/requires-approval controls. Covers loading, empty, error, transport-offline, mutation-error, and concurrent-refresh states with i18n labels in both catalogs (`en`/`cs`).\n\nNote: no standalone \"AGENT page\" with guidance/heartbeats blocks exists yet in `web/src`, so this lands as a tested, drop-in component ready to be composed into that page once it's built, rather than fabricating the rest of that page's scope.\n\nVerified in this run: backend build (all packages), dependency-boundary check, backend unit+integration tests (591 tests) and e2e tests (5 tests), web build, and web test suite (93 tests) — all passing.\n\nRelay-Step-Status: pass",
